            "answer": {
              "short": "$c=4$\n\nUse $BC=AB$ and retain the positive value of $c$.",
              "worked": "All sides of a rhombus are equal, so $BC^2=AB^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2-3)^2+(c-2)^2&=5\\\\(c-2)^2&=4\\\\c-2&=\\pm2\\\\c&=0\\text{ or }4\\end{align*}$$\nSince $c$ is positive, $c=4$.",
